1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
[Gentle, reflective piano chords playing]

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,400
♪ We scale the networks ♪

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,200
♪ We scale the clouds ♪

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,800
♪ Built shining systems ♪

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,200
♪ Loud enough to drown us out ♪

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,000
[Soft electronic beat enters]
♪ Every year another dashboard ♪

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,700
♪ Another update to survive ♪

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:23,500
♪ Another voice saying, "Move faster
if you wanna stay alive" ♪

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:30,000
♪ But somewhere in the noise, somebody
still cared enough to slow things down ♪

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,200
♪ A calm voice in the darkness saying, ♪

11
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,000
[Music pauses, vocals soften]
♪ "Take your time, I'll explain it again" ♪

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
[Music swells into an anthemic chorus]
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

13
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,800
♪ Not just the cold machinery ♪

14
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,500
♪ Not just the optimization ♪

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,000
♪ Or the endless urgency ♪

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,800
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

17
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,500
♪ In every thoughtful thing we do ♪

18
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:59,500
♪ Every doorway left open, every system
built for people passing through ♪

19
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,200
[Music softens to a gentle pulse]
♪ Somebody wrote the alt text ♪

20
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,200
♪ Somebody fixed the form ♪

21
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:12,000
♪ Somebody stayed late helping strangers
navigate another storm ♪

22
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:18,000
♪ Somebody made the interface
a little easier to trust ♪

23
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,800
♪ And maybe civilization is partly
built from things like us ♪

24
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:27,000
♪ Not heroes ♪

25
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
♪ Not visionaries ♪

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
[Music builds in intensity]
♪ Just people refusing to make
the world harder than it has to be ♪

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
[Powerful, uplifting chorus returns]
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,800
♪ Not just the cold machinery ♪

29
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,500
♪ Not just the optimization ♪

30
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,800
♪ Or the endless urgency ♪

31
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:50,800
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

32
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,500
♪ In every thoughtful thing we do ♪

33
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:59,500
♪ Every doorway left open, every system
built for people passing through ♪

34
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,500
[Drums drop out; warm piano and synths]
♪ I don't need a frictionless existence ♪

35
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:06,500
♪ I don't need to optimize my soul ♪

36
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:14,200
♪ I just want futures big enough
for tenderness and technology ♪

37
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,500
♪ That don't mistake exhaustion for failure ♪

38
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:25,000
[Rhythm builds toward a climax]
♪ And maybe the most human thing
we ever build, we ever build ♪

39
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
♪ Will be systems that remember
people are fragile ♪

40
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[Climactic, soaring final chorus]
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

41
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
♪ Soft lights across the circuitry ♪

42
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
♪ Warmth inside the architecture ♪

43
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
♪ Care inside complexity ♪

44
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,800
♪ Kindness scales too ♪

45
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:47,800
♪ And maybe that is how we make it through ♪

46
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,500
♪ Not by becoming machines ♪

47
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,200
♪ But by refusing to stop being human ♪

48
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:58,000
[Music stops; soft, intimate vocal]
♪ Take your time, I'll explain it again ♪
